#: ../../../tutorials/05-fused-softmax.md:1
msgid "5. Fused Softmax"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/05-fused-softmax.md:3
msgid "Softmax is a multi-step operation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/05-fused-softmax.md:5
msgid "softmax(x)_i = exp(x_i - max(x)) / Σ exp(x_j - max(x))\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/05-fused-softmax.md:9
msgid ""
"A naive implementation would use separate kernels for each step. **Kernel "
"fusion** combines all steps into one kernel to avoid redundant memory "
"traffic. Each kernel launch has overhead (~10–20 microseconds), and each "
"round-trip to global memory is slow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/05-fused-softmax.md:11
msgid ""
